# Build-time PUBLIC config for production (`next build` auto-loads this).
#
# These NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are NOT secrets — Next.js inlines them into the
# client bundle, so they're already visible to anyone using the deployed app.
# Committing them lets CI builds (Cloudflare Workers Builds) compile without
# needing build-vars configured in the dashboard.
#
# Real secrets (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET) are NOT here —
# they live as Cloudflare Worker runtime secrets.
#
# Local dev overrides these via .env.local / .env.production.local (higher precedence).

